{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03X7", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-etale-topos-independent-partial-universe}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-section-change-alpha}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca60d55ffaf69d6dbc2deea6a79fbede6ba193d3eca12377d5dfb0258c401c35", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor completeness we state and prove the invariance under choice of partial\nuniverse of the cohomology groups we are considering. We will prove invariance\nof the small <ACCENT_0001>tale topos in\nLemma <REF_0001> below.\nFor notation and terminology used in this lemma we refer to\nTopologies, Section <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98234fd2fc3e607145545d500404920a6bdcbe209b26355bde8b95333f4f5329", "unit_id": "tag:03X7:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03X7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\tau \\in \\{fppf, syntomic, smooth, \\etale, Zariski\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch'/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0005": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\Sch'/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0011": "$$\nH^p_\\tau(U, \\mathcal{F}'|_{(\\Sch/S)_\\tau}) =\nH^p_\\tau(U, \\mathcal{F}')\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0013": "$U$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0015": "$U$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0017": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{F}'$", "MATH_0019": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau'$", "MATH_0020": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-cohomology-enlarge-partial-universe}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6835386a08f068e186ef66f0fe5d6bca642e4b5238e7a06abccf5e4a5444e2e1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d33a5290a63aea2edcf81643830ffbc97538288002db719f2a10b04f629cee4d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> be two\nbig <MATH_0005>-sites of <MATH_0006>, and assume that the first is contained in the second.\nIn this case\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for any abelian sheaf <MATH_0007> defined on <MATH_0008> and\nany object <MATH_0009> of <MATH_0010> we have\n<MATH_0011>\nIn words: the cohomology of <MATH_0012> over <MATH_0013> computed in the bigger site\nagrees with the cohomology of <MATH_0014> restricted to the smaller site\nover <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0003> for any abelian sheaf <MATH_0016> on <MATH_0017> there is an\nabelian sheaf <MATH_0018> on <MATH_0019> whose restriction to\n<MATH_0020> is isomorphic to <MATH_0021>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:73e49d7a14ba89a97b5d24bafeaca6205dcdcd6160233cc4798deda4fbe88373", "unit_id": "tag:03YY:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03X7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau \\to (\\Sch'/S)_\\tau$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-change-alpha}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-bigger-site}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-cohomology-bigger-site}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0d0978753a02ba5b6857d44310e9db5008c84f812de6c413fdd132793c7a056d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a2e5c1c47c3b78583cc41ccf7313763393a3766e4ba8f8cef5240b3c069fa1f", "source_text": "By Topologies, Lemma <REF_0001> the inclusion functor\n<MATH_0001> satisfies the assumptions of\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>. This implies (2) and (1)\nfollows from\nCohomology on Sites, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ecfa356774bca4a84cfa3cffe1aaf47f4408fbe934ce6f1aa2914ac48376d275", "unit_id": "tag:03YY:proof"}
